  "text": "When I think about my financial situation, there's a bit of stress to it and so far as much as working almost 40 hours a week doing quite a bit for this restaurant.\n And even though the paycheck's pretty good, you know, the amount of effort and time and value that I'm sharing, I think, even though it goes very appreciated by the owner and manager. Doesn't always feel like it's appreciated by the team. And I feel like, you know, for the fact that, you know, there's problems with labor at work, like, I feel like I would deserve a raise, you know.\n But, you know, between that and trying to make the music work and make, you know, AI work, it's just a lot of long-term thinking, long-term conscious, gold-driven, you know, action. And it's just tiring, you know. And then I'm really hoping for the point where all the free time\n and spending and additioning all the money that I have to get from my main job to keep a roof over my head and, you know, food on my plate and all that. It would be nice to have all the creative stuff start to pay for things, you know. It's always been a big goal. And just putting a lot of time and energy into that to make that transition. And it's just a lot, you know.\n Yeah. Just tired. But I definitely feel like there's a lot of emotion right now. I feel very excited at the same time. It's why I'm still have energy to talk to you right now, to work on these things when I get home after midnight. Yeah. I mean, it feels like it's worth it and it's going somewhere. It's just, uh,\n always been a little impatient as well. The long-term thinking takes a lot of energy because it's not a as natural as the short-term thinking for me.",
  "status": "done",
